2.2,1956,48,101,24],[19601,15.9,1956,48,109,24]],"links":[["Mora County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/new-mexico/mora-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, January to February ran 30% of normal and May to June ran 192% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 26% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 19299 shows a preliminary August to September 2026 estimate of 188.9, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
